@@ -514,6 +514,17 @@ <h4>Required Binding Strength</h4>
 If the binding strength is required, the data element SHALL contain one of the values in the bound value set.
 </p>
 <p>
+For these bindings:
+</p>
+<ul>
+<li><b>code</b>: The code SHALL contain a code from the ValueSet</li>
+<li><b>Coding</b>: the system/code values SHALL identify one of the codes in the value set</li>
+<li><b>CodeableConcept</b>: at least one of the coding elements SHALL contain a system/code that is in the value set</li>
+</ul> 
+<p>
+Version may be required - depending on the code system and applicable local policies.
+</p>
+<p>
 Required binding strength is used for elements where the value needs to be strictly controlled so the element 
 can be interpreted with confidence. Required binding strength SHALL be used for elements with type code (unless 
 the element has a context-free (i.e., no binding.additional.usage present) 
